> New to filters? Start with [Filtering](/deploy/upgrades/filtering), which covers rules and groups.

Every rule starts with a field. Some are obvious, like Year, and some aren't, like Popularity or Cutoff Met. The tables below explain what each field actually checks, so come back here whenever you're building a rule and aren't sure which field you need.

## Shared Fields

<div class="mb-5">
<AdaptiveList
	data={sharedFields}
	columns={fieldColumns}>
	<!-- Renders text between backticks as inline code and text between asterisks in italics, like Markdown. -->
	{#snippet rich(text)}{#each text.split('`') as code, c}{#if c % 2}<code>{code}</code>{:else}{#each code.split('*') as part, i}{#if i % 2}<em>{part}</em>{:else}{part}{/if}{/each}{/if}{/each}{/snippet}
	{#snippet checks(row)}{@render rich(row.checks)}{#if row.seeAlso}{' '}See <a href={row.seeAlso.href}>{row.seeAlso.label}</a>.{/if}{/snippet}
	{#snippet cell(row, col)}
		{#if col.key === 'field'}
			<span class="font-medium">{row.field}</span>
		{:else if col.key === 'kind'}
			<code>{row.kind}</code>
		{:else}
			{@render checks(row)}
		{/if}
	{/snippet}
	{#snippet card(row)}
		<div class="font-medium">{row.field} <code class="text-sm font-normal">{row.kind}</code></div>
		<div class="mt-1 text-sm">{@render checks(row)}</div>
	{/snippet}
</AdaptiveList>
</div>

### Cutoff Met

**Cutoff Met** is a *special* boolean field. It evaulates to <u>true</u> when a file scores at least **Cutoff %** of its quality profile's Upgrade Until Custom Format Score. Cutoff % is a top level setting on the filter itself, and it applies to every Cutoff Met rule in that filter. For a series, the score is the average across all of its episode files.

For a file scoring `860,000` on Dictionarry's 1080p Quality profile, which stops upgrading at `1,000,000`:

- At 100%, it needs `1,000,000`, so Cutoff Met is False.
- At 80%, it needs `800,000`, so Cutoff Met is True.

